  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Identifying and Protecting VoTs in the Time of COVID-19 in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the Government of Sudan to respond to COVID-19 impacts on human trafficking through policy-oriented research, victim identification and continuation of critical protection services to Victims of Trafficking (VoTs). The project will work towards this project goal through the following objectives: Objective 1: The 2021-2023 NPA reflects and responds to research study recommendations on COVID-19 impacts and trends on human trafficking. Objective 2: Frontline officers and migrant community leaders are equipped with the skills to better screen, identify and support VoTs among the migrants who have been made more vulnerable due to COVID-19 impacts. Objective 3: VoTs have access to medical and psychosocial support and an option of voluntary and safe repatriation to their countries of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
